    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added `toDisplay(String)`, which splits the E.164 number into its country code (using the existing known-country-code table) and national digits, then joins the country code and the national digits grouped in threes with spaces, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. I refactored the country-code matching into a shared `matchLongestCountryCode` helper reused by the existing validation logic. Non-E.164 values are returned unchanged; unknown country codes group the full number.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` mapping that delegates to `TelephoneNormalizer.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (asserting `telephone` = `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).",
